EnrollmentService.enroll() calls repo.create() inside try { ... } catch, and maps DuplicateEnrollmentError to { ok: false, error: "already_enrolled" }. Its test (Vitest 3.x):

const repo = {
  create: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ id: "e1", userId: "u1", courseId: "ts-101", status: "active", progress: 0, enrolledAt: "2026-10-26T08:14:03.000Z" }),
  findById: vi.fn(), findByUser: vi.fn(), update: vi.fn(), delete: vi.fn(),
};
const service = new EnrollmentService(repo, clock);
const first = await service.enroll("u1", "ts-101");
await service.enroll("u1", "ts-101");
expect(first.ok).toBe(true);
expect(repo.create).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);

Statement: "If someone deletes the catch block from enroll(), this test fails."

A teammate's in-memory fake and a new service method:

class FakeEnrollmentRepository implements EnrollmentRepository {
  private rows = new Map<string, Enrollment>();
  async findById(id: string) { return this.rows.get(id) ?? null; }
  // create, findByUser, update, delete ...
}

async complete(id: string) {            // in EnrollmentService
  const e = await this.repo.findById(id);
  if (!e) return null;
  e.progress = 100;
  e.status = "completed";
  return e;
}

The test passes with the fake:

await service.complete("e1");
expect((await repo.findById("e1"))?.status).toBe("completed");

Statement: "With PostgresEnrollmentRepository the same assertion would fail, because complete() never writes the change back with update()."
